1
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:06,630
This tiny square is about

2
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:07,740
the size of a postage

3
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:08,730
stamp.

4
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:10,020
Inside it are more than

5
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:12,110
a hundred billion switches.

6
00:00:12,110 --> 00:00:13,370
And every single one was

7
00:00:13,370 --> 00:00:15,120
drawn… with light.

8
00:00:16,175 --> 00:00:16,965
Last time,

9
00:00:16,965 --> 00:00:18,315
I asked why a compost

10
00:00:18,315 --> 00:00:20,185
bin gets warm inside.

11
00:00:20,185 --> 00:00:21,865
Tiny decomposers break down the

12
00:00:21,865 --> 00:00:23,055
food scraps,

13
00:00:23,055 --> 00:00:23,905
and as they work,

14
00:00:23,905 --> 00:00:25,335
they give off heat.

15
00:00:25,335 --> 00:00:26,255
A busy bin is a

16
00:00:26,255 --> 00:00:27,745
warm bin!

17
00:00:27,981 --> 00:00:30,152
In November 2026,

18
00:00:30,152 --> 00:00:32,271
the computer chip company Nvidia

19
00:00:32,271 --> 00:00:33,381
was in the news around

20
00:00:33,381 --> 00:00:34,411
the world.

21
00:00:34,411 --> 00:00:35,031
Its founder,

22
00:00:35,031 --> 00:00:36,212
Jensen Huang,

23
00:00:36,212 --> 00:00:37,531
stepped down as its boss

24
00:00:37,531 --> 00:00:39,001
for a short time.

25
00:00:39,001 --> 00:00:39,322
Then,

26
00:00:39,322 --> 00:00:40,582
eleven days later,

27
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:42,582
he came back as CEO.

28
00:00:42,582 --> 00:00:43,972
Why does the whole world

29
00:00:43,972 --> 00:00:45,322
watch one chip company so

30
00:00:45,322 --> 00:00:46,432
closely?

31
00:00:46,432 --> 00:00:47,631
Because its chips are the

32
00:00:47,631 --> 00:00:50,261
engines that run today's AI.

33
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,110
Nvidia's famous chips are called

34
00:00:53,110 --> 00:00:54,250
GPUs,

35
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:56,290
graphics processing units.

36
00:00:56,290 --> 00:00:57,220
They were first made to

37
00:00:57,220 --> 00:00:58,940
draw video games.

38
00:00:58,940 --> 00:01:00,250
A picture on a screen

39
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:01,420
is made of millions of

40
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:03,730
tiny dots called pixels.

41
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:04,530
To draw it,

42
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:05,640
the computer works out the

43
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:07,250
colour of every dot,

44
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:09,490
many times every second.

45
00:01:09,733 --> 00:01:11,463
An ordinary computer brain,

46
00:01:11,463 --> 00:01:12,693
a CPU,

47
00:01:12,693 --> 00:01:14,053
is like one very clever

48
00:01:14,053 --> 00:01:14,913
teacher,

49
00:01:14,913 --> 00:01:17,383
solving sums one after another.

50
00:01:17,383 --> 00:01:18,533
A GPU is like a

51
00:01:18,533 --> 00:01:20,583
whole school hall of pupils,

52
00:01:20,583 --> 00:01:22,553
each solving one small sum,

53
00:01:22,553 --> 00:01:24,433
all at the same time.

54
00:01:24,674 --> 00:01:25,894
And it turns out AI

55
00:01:25,894 --> 00:01:27,714
learns in a similar way:

56
00:01:27,714 --> 00:01:29,374
by doing billions and billions

57
00:01:29,374 --> 00:01:31,434
of small multiplications.

58
00:01:31,434 --> 00:01:32,334
So the chip built for

59
00:01:32,334 --> 00:01:34,094
games became the chip that

60
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:36,074
helps teach AI.

61
00:01:36,317 --> 00:01:37,557
In Primary Five,

62
00:01:37,557 --> 00:01:39,817
you learn about electric circuits.

63
00:01:39,817 --> 00:01:41,157
When the switch is closed,

64
00:01:41,157 --> 00:01:42,357
current flows and the bulb

65
00:01:42,357 --> 00:01:43,497
lights up.

66
00:01:43,497 --> 00:01:44,757
When the switch is open,

67
00:01:44,757 --> 00:01:45,517
there is a gap,

68
00:01:45,517 --> 00:01:47,597
and no current flows.

69
00:01:47,848 --> 00:01:48,708
A chip is made of

70
00:01:48,708 --> 00:01:51,428
tiny switches called transistors.

71
00:01:51,428 --> 00:01:53,428
They have no moving parts.

72
00:01:53,428 --> 00:01:54,718
On or off.

73
00:01:54,718 --> 00:01:56,178
One or zero.

74
00:01:56,178 --> 00:01:57,708
Billions of switches,

75
00:01:57,708 --> 00:01:59,098
flicking on and off billions

76
00:01:59,098 --> 00:02:00,588
of times a second.

77
00:02:00,588 --> 00:02:01,438
That is how a chip

78
00:02:01,438 --> 00:02:02,868
works things out.

79
00:02:02,868 --> 00:02:03,658
So how do you build

80
00:02:03,658 --> 00:02:05,838
a hundred billion switches?

81
00:02:05,838 --> 00:02:07,548
Let's find out.

82
00:02:07,784 --> 00:02:09,044
Are you ready?

83
00:02:09,044 --> 00:02:10,084
Three!

84
00:02:10,084 --> 00:02:11,074
Two!

85
00:02:11,074 --> 00:02:12,074
One!

86
00:02:12,074 --> 00:02:13,234
Go!

87
00:02:17,225 --> 00:02:17,915
You are a grain of

88
00:02:17,915 --> 00:02:19,185
sand.

89
00:02:19,431 --> 00:02:21,211
Sand is mostly silica,

90
00:02:21,211 --> 00:02:23,361
made of silicon and oxygen.

91
00:02:23,361 --> 00:02:24,991
You are cleaned and melted

92
00:02:24,991 --> 00:02:26,161
until you are almost pure

93
00:02:26,161 --> 00:02:27,451
silicon.

94
00:02:27,693 --> 00:02:29,153
A tiny seed crystal is

95
00:02:29,153 --> 00:02:30,223
dipped into you and pulled

96
00:02:30,223 --> 00:02:31,303
up slowly,

97
00:02:31,303 --> 00:02:33,253
turning round and round.

98
00:02:33,253 --> 00:02:34,493
You grow into a shiny

99
00:02:34,493 --> 00:02:35,973
cylinder of crystal,

100
00:02:35,973 --> 00:02:36,973
as long as a child

101
00:02:36,973 --> 00:02:38,193
is tall.

102
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:39,680
You are sliced into thin

103
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:41,610
round plates called wafers,

104
00:02:41,610 --> 00:02:42,660
thinner than a coin,

105
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:44,570
and polished until you shine

106
00:02:44,570 --> 00:02:45,910
like a mirror.

107
00:02:46,164 --> 00:02:47,224
Now you enter a clean

108
00:02:47,224 --> 00:02:48,134
room.

109
00:02:48,134 --> 00:02:49,614
The air here is cleaner

110
00:02:49,614 --> 00:02:51,954
than a hospital operating theatre.

111
00:02:51,954 --> 00:02:53,484
The workers wear suits that

112
00:02:53,484 --> 00:02:54,434
cover them from head to

113
00:02:54,434 --> 00:02:55,574
toe.

114
00:03:00,223 --> 00:03:01,403
In Primary Four,

115
00:03:01,403 --> 00:03:02,763
you learn that light travels

116
00:03:02,763 --> 00:03:04,133
in a straight line,

117
00:03:04,133 --> 00:03:05,273
and when an object blocks

118
00:03:05,273 --> 00:03:05,863
light,

119
00:03:05,863 --> 00:03:07,633
it forms a shadow.

120
00:03:08,930 --> 00:03:09,800
You are coated with a

121
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,890
special layer that changes when

122
00:03:11,890 --> 00:03:13,470
light shines on it.

123
00:03:13,470 --> 00:03:14,110
A stencil,

124
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:14,960
called a mask,

125
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:16,600
blocks some of the light.

126
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:17,920
Where the light reaches you,

127
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,590
the layer changes.

128
00:03:19,590 --> 00:03:20,920
Where the mask blocks it,

129
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:23,040
the shadow keeps the pattern.

130
00:03:24,090 --> 00:03:25,780
Lenses shrink the pattern again

131
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:26,760
and again,

132
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:28,430
until each line is thousands

133
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:29,420
of times thinner than a

134
00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:30,560
hair.

135
00:03:30,813 --> 00:03:31,933
Then the pattern is etched

136
00:03:31,933 --> 00:03:32,503
in,

137
00:03:32,503 --> 00:03:33,423
metal is added,

138
00:03:33,423 --> 00:03:34,993
and it starts again.

139
00:03:34,993 --> 00:03:36,093
Layer on layer,

140
00:03:36,093 --> 00:03:37,063
hundreds of steps,

141
00:03:37,063 --> 00:03:38,693
over many weeks.

142
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:39,630
At the end,

143
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:41,850
one wafer holds many chips.

144
00:03:41,850 --> 00:03:42,940
They are cut apart,

145
00:03:42,940 --> 00:03:43,420
tested,

146
00:03:43,420 --> 00:03:45,490
and packed into a case.

147
00:03:45,490 --> 00:03:47,280
Now you are a chip!

148
00:03:47,523 --> 00:03:49,323
Nvidia designs its chips in

149
00:03:49,323 --> 00:03:50,703
the United States,

150
00:03:50,703 --> 00:03:52,663
and factories in Taiwan build

151
00:03:52,663 --> 00:03:54,103
the newest ones.

152
00:03:54,103 --> 00:03:55,613
And Singapore?

153
00:03:55,613 --> 00:03:57,133
About one in every ten

154
00:03:57,133 --> 00:03:58,233
chips in the world is

155
00:03:58,233 --> 00:03:59,503
made here.

156
00:04:00,553 --> 00:04:02,373
When thousands of GPUs work

157
00:04:02,373 --> 00:04:04,193
together to train an AI,

158
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:04,993
they use a lot of

159
00:04:04,993 --> 00:04:06,123
electricity,

160
00:04:06,123 --> 00:04:07,543
and they get hot.

161
00:04:07,543 --> 00:04:07,983
Remember,

162
00:04:07,983 --> 00:04:09,433
heat flows from a hotter

163
00:04:09,433 --> 00:04:11,333
object to a colder one.

164
00:04:11,333 --> 00:04:12,553
So cool water and air

165
00:04:12,553 --> 00:04:13,993
flow past the chips to

166
00:04:13,993 --> 00:04:15,533
carry the heat away.

167
00:04:15,533 --> 00:04:17,133
Engineers are working hard to

168
00:04:17,133 --> 00:04:18,553
use less energy,

169
00:04:18,553 --> 00:04:20,163
so AI can grow without

170
00:04:20,163 --> 00:04:22,163
wasting electricity.

171
00:04:22,412 --> 00:04:24,232
Try this with your class.

172
00:04:24,232 --> 00:04:25,962
Give one friend twenty easy

173
00:04:25,962 --> 00:04:27,512
sums to do alone.

174
00:04:27,512 --> 00:04:28,772
Then give twenty friends one

175
00:04:28,772 --> 00:04:30,032
sum each.

176
00:04:30,032 --> 00:04:31,632
Who finishes first?

177
00:04:31,632 --> 00:04:32,802
That is the difference between

178
00:04:32,802 --> 00:04:35,542
a CPU and a GPU!

179
00:04:35,787 --> 00:04:37,177
Think about it!

180
00:04:37,177 --> 00:04:37,997
Why do you think chip

181
00:04:37,997 --> 00:04:40,327
factories must be even cleaner

182
00:04:40,327 --> 00:04:42,827
than a hospital operating theatre?

183
00:04:42,827 --> 00:04:43,777
I'll tell you the answer

184
00:04:43,777 --> 00:04:45,237
next time.

185
00:04:45,488 --> 00:04:47,578
A hundred billion switches.

186
00:04:47,578 --> 00:04:49,458
Drawn with light and shadow.

187
00:04:49,458 --> 00:04:50,348
And it all started with

188
00:04:50,348 --> 00:04:51,968
a grain of sand.

189
00:04:52,983 --> 00:04:55,142
Now you know!
